# The vendored SDK is checked byte for byte, so git must not touch its bytes.
#
# This repository is worked on from Windows, where the default is to store LF
# and hand out CRLF. For every other file that is invisible and harmless. For
# vendor/supabase.js it is not: tools/check-vendor.mjs compares its sha256
# against the digest recorded in vendor/README.md, and a fresh clone would get
# a file with different line endings, a different digest, and a failing check
# that looks exactly like the tampering the check exists to find.
#
# -text means "leave this alone in both directions".
vendor/supabase.js -text
